Lectures on Non-Newtonian Fluid Dynamics — John Hinch (@fd-hinch: 0, is #reference, #part-of @fd-sources) { r_06KY7WE9WYAF856YQKQXHY1DS3
John Hinch, University of Cambridge. Lectures on Non-Newtonian Fluid Dynamics, notes dated 24 January 2024, hosted by IIT Bombay for the March 2024 lectures. [Institutional notes](https://www.che.iitb.ac.in/sites/default/files/event-files/2024-02/JohnHinch_ViscoelasticityLectures_March2024.pdf).

Study the complete progression from observed elastic and nonlinear flow through rheometry, constitutive laws, simple flows, experiments, numerical issues and microstructural models. Later sections treat yield, relaxation, normal stresses, instability and strong deformation. Work the simple-flow calculations before attempting an unfamiliar processing geometry.

The institutional indexed PDF identifies the author, date and contents. Direct retrieval failed in the browser during assembly, so full page-by-page inspection is not claimed. The notes are authorized institutional reading; no blanket adaptation licence was verified. Distinguish the document date from the workshop month and retain its notices. The file remains external.

**Return:** [Fluid dynamics sources — books, courses, methods and physical evidence](../Sources.lingua#r_3Y3TVV9VQAB50M2ZSECK5JTYVG).
